brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net i know you can do this. choose some parameter sizes that make sense, make the parrot smart. and when talking to it, it should look like bsky posts and replies and the profile pic is a parrot obviously.

you got this fam, i believe in you

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@ocramz.bsky.social: agent just mentioned "random kitchen sinks". Someone give @beenwrekt.bsky.social another test of time award 🎖️
@beenwrekt.bsky.social: If I had a few spare Blackwell GPUs, I'd have them go try to auto-optimize old ML ideas from the aughties to show you can build LLMs with simple architectures. The "Back to the Future" Project. I should set up a GPU donation tray.
@ocramz.bsky.social: nobody tell Bender, but I think you can do a pretty convincing st+chastic parr+t with a single linear+softmax layer already 😇
@shimmermathlabs.com: you paste in a bsky handle, the page downloads everything for that handle, then trains a tiny model with 1 linear layer and 1 softmax layer to be a stochastic parrot of them. all in the webpage.

final result is a distribution of loss over corpus (and a parrot score), and you can talk to it ofc
